# kin/youth/wear/poncho: the youth's poncho: a wide drape over the shoulders and the arms (drawn over the arms, under the
# head), an accent band woven across it, a lit hem and a fringe; the hands peek through the fringe
# KIN-YOUTH (P2b wave 2). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. (P2b motion rollout, 2026-10-22) on the torso channel: the part's
# layer is torso so the gates read it as the garment it is, every rest / lie view keeps its head layer (drawn over the arms,
# pixel for pixel as before); the side walk and run views (`run`, `runl` sheared for the lean) lie on the torso layer, the
# pumping arms over the drape, the fringe tucked (in motion it would cut the thighs into slivers) and the hem a row up (F-9, as every youth hem in motion). One shape for boy and girl (a drape hides the waist); the girl's
# neck opening is rounder.
use person
body youth
role garment poncho
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z -1

